				<blockquote class="messageText SelectQuoteContainer ugc baseHtml">
					
					<div style="text-align: center"><b><img src="https://i.imgur.gg/Zhc4DUd-folder.jpg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://i.imgur.gg/Zhc4DUd-folder.jpg" style="">  <br>
<br>
Madonna - Music: Instrumentals (2000) <b>| </b>AAC 256kbps / 44.1kHz</b><br>
<i><b><br>
Music</b></i> is the eighth studio album by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Americans" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">American</a> singer and songwriter <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a>, released on September 18, 2000, by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(company)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Maverick</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warner_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Warner Bros. Records</a>. Following the success of her previous album <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ray_of_Light" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Ray of Light</a></i> (1998), Madonna found herself in a music scene increasingly influenced by a younger generation of singers such as <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Britney_Spears" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Britney Spears</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Aguilera" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Christina Aguilera</a>. This led her to seek a distinctive sound that would set her apart in the evolving musical landscape. Her collaborations with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirwais_Ahmadza%C3%AF" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Mirwais Ahmadzaï</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Orbit" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">William Orbit</a> resulted in a more <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Experimental_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">experimental</a> direction for the album. <i>Music</i> incorporates many different genres into its overall <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance-pop" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">dance-pop</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronica" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">electronica</a> vibe, taking influences from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">funk</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">house</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Techno_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">techno</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">rock</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">country</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Folk_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">folk</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R&amp;B" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">R&amp;B</a>. With the album embracing a western motif, Madonna reimagined her image in the role of a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cowgirl" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">cowgirl</a>.<br>
